{
  "scriptText": "am I the jerk for walking out of dinner after my girlfriend \"tested\" me? I (29M) have been dating my girlfriend (28F) for 8 months. She's really into social media and relationship \"tests,\" which I've always found kind of cringe but harmless. Last night we went out to dinner. Halfway through the meal, a woman came up to our table, flirted with me, and asked for my number. I immediately said no and told her I was there with my girlfriend. After the woman left, my girlfriend started laughing and told me it was her friend and she wanted to see how I'd react. She said I \"passed,\" so I shouldn't be mad. I was pissed. I told her that was humiliating and manipulative, and I don't want to be tested like I'm on some reality show. She said I was overreacting and that other guys would find it funny. I paid for my food, left, and went home. Now she says I embarrassed her and made a big deal out of nothing. am I the jerk for walking out? So... Am I the jerk here?",
